## Decision sheet

|         Decision          |                            Contract and rationale                            | Evidence and next experiment |
| ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |
| Deployment ownership      | Configure only; caller supplies endpoint, credentials and trust              | FIXME qualify installation and bootstrap boundaries |
| Transport and privilege   | HTTP on the execution host                                                   | FIXME authentication and permission probes |
| Identity and refused rows | Definition-owned identifier, natural key, case rule and exclusions           | FIXME uniqueness, rename and built-in objects |
| Absence                   | Definition selects documented by-key absence or verified complete listing    | FIXME absence response and pagination end rule |
| Field ownership           | Declared fields; omission/null unmanaged; explicit clears                    | FIXME defaults, normalisation and partial update |
| References                | Names resolved before writing; null foreign keys project as empty references | FIXME ambiguity and relationship ownership |
| Activation                | Add an apply module only where saved and active state differ                 | FIXME scope, completion and observable active state |
| Writer coordination       | Caller serializes writers; no lock promised                                  | FIXME conflicts, atomicity and partial recovery |
| Secrets                   | Public allowlist; write-only fields need an explicit rotation contract       | FIXME listings, read-back and independent acceptance probe |
| Version probe             | Cached read before a planned mutation, including check prediction            | FIXME version privilege, series and operation exclusions |
| Lab                       | External endpoint in Molecule; loopback fake in integration                  | FIXME full lifecycle and cleanup evidence |

